From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: samsung-dual-battery: link to the supplies it holds

The driver holds its charger, fuel gauge and limiter power supplies for
as long as it is bound and polls them. Nothing ties its lifetime to
theirs: unbinding one of them, or unloading its module, left this driver
with a power supply whose callbacks were gone, and the next poll called
into freed code. Add a managed device link to each supply's device, so
the driver core unbinds this driver first and probes it again once the
supply is back. A supply registers from its driver's probe, so wait
until that driver is bound: a link to a supplier still probing made the
cleanup after a deferred probe warn.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/samsung-dual-battery.c |   14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)


diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/samsung-dual-battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/samsung-dual-battery.c
index f18cf6f..29df908 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/samsung-dual-battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/samsung-dual-battery.c
@@ -327,6 +327,20 @@ static int sdb_get_psy(struct device *dev, const char *prop,
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(*psy), "%s\n", prop);
 	if (!*psy)
 		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+
+	/*
+	 * The supply is held and polled for as long as this driver is bound.
+	 * A managed link unbinds this driver before the supply's driver goes
+	 * away and probes it again once it is back, so the reference never
+	 * outlives the callbacks behind it (unloading the charger module
+	 * otherwise left this driver calling into freed code).
+	 */
+	/* a supply registers from its driver's probe: link once that is done */
+	if (!device_is_bound((*psy)->dev.parent))
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+	if (!device_link_add(dev, (*psy)->dev.parent, DL_FLAG_AUTOPROBE_CONSUMER))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "no device link to %s\n",
+				     dev_name((*psy)->dev.parent));
 	return 0;
 }
 
